{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"color wheel structure for game art color wheel structure for game art","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","fileName":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:18\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Color Design for Game Environments]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Color Design for Game Environments","Analogous Environment Palette","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"color wheel structure for game art color wheel structure for game art","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","fileName":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art","heading":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A color wheel arranges hues by their relationship around a circle, making primary, secondary, and tertiary combinations visible. The exact primaries depend on whether the system describes emitted light, pigment, or another color model.\n\nFor environment art, the wheel is a planning device rather than a rule that selects colors automatically. It helps the artist build [[Analogous Environment Palette|neighboring]], complementary, triadic, and tetradic relationships while still testing them in the intended lighting and context.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Color Design for Game Environments","Analogous Environment Palette","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"color wheel structure for game art color wheel structure for game art","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","fileName":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Color Wheel Structure for Game Art","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Color Design for Game Environments","Analogous Environment Palette","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}